Sonar Harness
Local Pre-Commit Quality Gate with Copilot-Driven Remediation
1. Purpose
The Sonar Harness is a local, pre-commit quality gate that detects new SonarAnalyzer.CSharp violations and uses GitHub Copilot Agent to assist with automated remediation.
It shifts Sonar validation from a post-commit or CI activity to the developer's local workflow. The harness detects issues, enriches them with SonarQube rule information when available, assists with remediation, requires developer approval, and validates the changes again before the commit is allowed to proceed.
Core workflow:
Detect → Explain → Remediate → Approve → Revalidate → Commit
2. Prerequisites[AD1.1][HS1.2]
Note: This workflow is currently designed to work with GitHub Copilot only. 
2.1 Git Hooks
The repository uses Git's native hooks mechanism rather than Husky or npm-based hooks.
git config core.hooksPath .githooks
The pre-commit workflow is triggered from:
.githooks/pre-commit
2.2 PowerShell
Either of the following must be available on PATH:
•	pwsh — PowerShell 7+
•	powershell.exe — Windows PowerShell
If neither executable is available, the pre-commit hook blocks the commit.
2.3 .NET SDK
A .NET SDK compatible with the projects under src/ is required.
dotnet build
2.4 VS Code CLI
The VS Code CLI (code) is required only when automatic Copilot Agent remediation should be launched.
code --version
If unavailable, remediation can be generated without launching VS Code:
pwsh -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File tools/sonar-remediate.ps1 -NoLaunch
2.5 Optional SonarQube Access
SonarQube access is optional. It is used only to enrich analyzer violations with additional rule information.
Variable	Required	Description
SONAR_HOST_URL	Optional	Base URL of the SonarQube server
SONAR_TOKEN	Optional	SonarQube user/analysis token
SONAR_PROJECT_KEY	Optional	SonarQube project key; defaults to WizNG.Web

If SonarQube variables are not configured, the enrichment step continues without SonarQube metadata. The local analyzer gate remains fully functional.
